    "body": "I tested this locally and think there are a few things that we need to think about a bit more.\r\n\r\nThis seems to treat all values as strings, which means that this doesn't work if you try to enable or disable a module, for example,\r\n```\r\n❯ cargo run config kubernetes.disabled false\r\n```\r\nHowever the value in the config is a string\r\n```\r\n❯ cat ~/.config/starship.toml \r\n...\r\n[kubernetes]\r\ndisabled = 'false'\r\n```\r\nso the module is not enabled.\r\n\r\nAlso if you run it with the incorrect argument it panics, would it be possible to print a nice error message.\r\n```\r\n❯ cargo run config foo 1  \r\n...\r\nthread 'main' panicked at 'index out of bounds: the len is 1 but the index is 1', /rustc/b8cedc00407a4c56a3bda1ed605c6fc166655447/src/libcore/slice/mod.rs:2791:10\r\nnote: run with `RUST_BACKTRACE=1` environment variable to display a backtrace\r\n```",
